Thought:  The `CUDA out of memory` error still persists despite changing the optimizer and reducing the learning rate. This suggests that the model's architecture or the way it is being used might be inherently memory-intensive. Given that DistilBERT is a smaller variant of BERT, it typically requires less memory than BERT, but there are still optimizations we can apply.

One approach is to reduce the sequence length of the input data. Longer sequences require more memory during processing. We will modify the script to reduce the maximum sequence length from 512 to 128 and re-run the training process.

